 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.62,
   "text": "If the Hubble telescope were aimed at the Earth, how detailed would the images be?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 3.86,
   "end": 6.22,
   "text": "The fundamental problem is that Hubble is too slow.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 6.7,
   "end": 10.06,
   "text": "Let me explain. Hubble routinely swivels to follow targets as it orbits.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 10.48,
   "end": 13.3,
   "text": "Usually the targets are astronomical objects that are super far away.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 13.66,
   "end": 17.74,
   "text": "The automatic onboard tracking algorithms can at best handle targets as close as about",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 17.74,
   "end": 20.92,
   "text": "10 times the distance to the moon. When astronomers want to use Hubble to take",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 20.92,
   "end": 24.16,
   "text": "pictures of the moon itself, they have to send it manual commands to rotate.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 24.48,
   "end": 28.06,
   "text": "It doesn't work very well. The resulting photos are better than what you can see",
   "avg_logprob": -0.082,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 28.06,
   "end": 31.12,
   "text": "with the naked eye, but they're not very good by Hubble standards.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 31.58,
   "end": 34.58,
   "text": "To track the surface of the Earth, Hubble would need to rotate at less than one",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 34.58,
   "end": 37.06,
   "text": "degree per second, or around a tenth of an RPM.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 37.68,
   "end": 40.98,
   "text": "But Hubble is simply too slow. It wasn't built for surface tracking.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 41.34,
   "end": 43.76,
   "text": "Clearly, we need our own targeting control system.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 44.26,
   "end": 47.48,
   "text": "With our custom system in place, Hubble could be made to track the surface and",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 47.48,
   "end": 49.94,
   "text": "get photos pretty close to its optimal quality.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 50.3,
   "end": 52.74,
   "text": "Which means that while Hubble couldn't read over your shoulder,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 53.06,
   "end": 55.32,
   "text": "it could watch you roll around on your desk chair.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.061,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.078
  },
  {
   "start": 55.32,
   "end": 58.26,
   "text": "But this isn't just a hypothetical situation.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.044
  },
  {
   "start": 58.92,
   "end": 62.58,
   "text": "Much of the technology in military spy satellites is believed to be similar to",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.044
  },
  {
   "start": 62.58,
   "end": 65.76,
   "text": "that of Hubble. So in a sense, pointing a Hubble-type",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.044
  },
  {
   "start": 65.76,
   "end": 67.9,
   "text": "telescope at the Earth's surface is not only possible,",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.044
  },
  {
   "start": 68.34,
   "end": 70.36,
   "text": "it's what the U.S. government actually does.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.114,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.044
  }
 ],
